    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Simplify fetch exceptions]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40802</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40802"/>
        <updated>2025-08-20T00:18:20.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/432915?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">The documentation for <code class="notranslate">fetch</code> includes a table in the "Exceptions" section with little examples for lots of the exceptions that can be thrown. We usually don't do this.</p>
<p dir="auto">Also, most of the exceptions listed are some version of "options properties were invalid according to the rules given in <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/RequestInit" rel="nofollow">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/RequestInit</a>" - it's better surely to state these rules once, in that page, and then say here that the exception is thrown if these rules are broken.<br>
(for one thing, we are inconsistent: for instance, we say that <code class="notranslate">method</code> must be valid according to its definition, but not that <code class="notranslate">credentials</code> must be valid).</p>
<p dir="auto">Maaaybe we ought to keep these examples, or some of them, in the "Examples" section. I'm not sure they are that useful though.</p>]]></content>
